WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 2: Exploring Space.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:10.960
Unit 2 pairs two information texts about astronomy and
life on the space station with The Burrow Discovery,

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.480
a story about a school science fair.

4
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.420
You will study twenty-five words such as
burrow, boycott, glare, cooperate and ownership,

5
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:25.000
and you will master indefinite pronouns,
singular agreement and adverbial phrases.

6
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:32.860
You will separate fact from opinion, compare biography with
autobiography, and write a friendly blog post of your own.

7
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:39.040
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:45.440
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
use the twenty-five Unit 2 words about science,

9
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:50.260
systems and social values accurately in speech and writing.

10
00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:57.980
You will also identify indefinite pronouns in a text
and use them with the matching singular or plural verb.

11
00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:05.280
You will also read an information text about astronomy
and extract main points supported by evidence.

12
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.620
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:16.340
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: occur,
occupy, convenience, correspond, equip, density.

14
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.040
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.840
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.020
The reading sequence includes The Night
Sky Above Us and Life on the Space Station.

17
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.720
Read actively.

18
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:37.560
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.600
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:47.820
The first language focus is Indefinite pronouns:
talking about people and things in general.

21
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:53.980
Indefinite pronouns stand in for people or
things when we do not need to name them exactly.

22
00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:59.860
One short word can replace a whole list,
which keeps writing smooth and clear.

23
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:06.300
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.280
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Astronaut interview role-play.

25
00:02:12.653 --> 00:02:16.660
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.320
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.920
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.720
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.360
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.100
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:42.660
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
